From 5c7392f5282a8e55f97f0e66709d4b0063cfb1ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 08:45:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Scope item 3-8 to the cascade: which rule defeats the shape

The update-target census said 98.1% of the corpus's ++/-- steps are on a
local the analysis did not prove numeric, with 6.76 M of the 7.05 M real
boxes in NavierStokes' ++currentRow family. Scoping the fix needs the
next thing down: not which names were dropped, which the waterfall
already counts, but which RULE defeats the shape the traffic is in --
because the rules want different fixes and two of them can never be
widened at all.

The update-target census is itself the oracle, and this is the
discrimination it was built for: a numeric local compiles c++ to a
native add and contributes no row, a local that stayed a JSValue
contributes LocalSlot, a captured one contributes LocalCell. Eight
shapes, one per conjunct.

Three suspects are innocent. A nested function declaration does not
defeat the enclosing local -- CanScalarReplaceLocals tolerates it, and
NavierStokes' FluidField is built out of them. Item 3-7's hoisting rule
produces a LocalCell, and NavierStokes reports 9 461 760 LocalSlot steps
against six LocalCell, so the conjunct that is correctness is not what
costs the boxes. And passing the value in as an argument trades
OtherName for Parameter and lands in the same row.

What is left is one conjunct: the analysis is per-function and will not
type a name from outside it. The sharp fixture is that this holds even
when the enclosing name is ALREADY PROVEN NUMERIC -- a conclusion is not
carried across a closure boundary. That is pure analysis reach with no
soundness argument attached, and it splits the work into a static half
(import the enclosing scope's proven-numeric set, which does not reach
NavierStokes because its root is held by 3-7's correctness rule) and a
run-time half (one IsNumber test where the value enters, which is the
only thing that does).

Tests only; no engine change. NumericLocalDefeatTests, 8 fixtures.
